     I'm playing the NetHack 3.0pl7 distribution from apple.com, and first
of all, I wanted to thank the development team for their great work.  NetHack's
responsible for far more lost productivity than any game I've found so far. :)
     I did come across a few bugs that I didn't see previously mentioned,
though:
     (By the way, these are on a 5-meg IIci in 1-bit mode.)
     1) When you dip a scroll into a potion to get a scroll of blank paper, it
becomes an unidentified scroll if you haven't found a scroll of blank paper
before.  The interesting thing about this is that it means that the scroll
title miraculously changes in the inventory when you dip the scroll (from, say,
"READ ME" to "HACKEM MUCHE"); I can understand how writing could be erased, but
I don't understand how the ink of the title miraculously survives and shifts
position like that. :)  (Of course, I can never understand why a scroll of
blank paper would have a title anyway, so maybe this is just me...)
     2) Mimics are 100% identifiable.  (This may be a feature. :) )  If you use
the / command and identify the space with the mimic, it says "I've never heard
of such items" rather than identifying whatever shape the mimic is imitating.
     3) "Just show scores" doesn't work; it returns to the Finder immediately.

